BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Victorian Cult of Mourning with Virginia Van Vliet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T150000
UID:6ad24d9cde300e00451ad86c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​After the death of Prince Albert\, Queen Victoria became kn
 own as “The Widow of Windsor”\, setting the tone for elaborate mournin
 g customs throughout the Empire.\nCome to learn about hair jewelry\, mutes
 \, crepe veils\, zinc tombstones\, tear bottles\, post mortem photography 
 and other elements of the Cult of Mourning.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Wychwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad24d9cde300e00451ad86c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Modern Careers: Unlocking New AI Career Paths
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T150000
UID:6ada329a198b996a80a897bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join one of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence\,  Sangeetha Dik
 shit and guest speaker Bhumika Arora for this interactive discussion.\nArt
 ificial intelligence is changing more than just how software gets built. I
 t is creating brand new ways to work across every industry. From tech role
 s evolving with AI tools to flexible remote gigs and new opportunities in 
 non-technical fields\, AI offers unique options for early-career professio
 nals and students entering the workforce. Join our guest speaker Bhumika 
 Arora in this interactive session that helps you understand the current A
 I job landscape and build a clear strategy for your future.\nSangeetha\nDi
 kshit\nis one of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is a Career and Lea
 dership Coach empowering individuals to navigate career transitions\, deve
 lop in-demand skills\, and achieve professional success.\nBhumika Arora\ni
 s a Career & Business Coach and AI Transformation Advisor. Bhumika works w
 ith individuals pursuing transitions into tech and customer success roles.
  Bhumika also collaborates with AI‑centric organizations as an Advisory 
 Partner\, contributing to initiatives related to emerging technologies and
  workforce development.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in R
 esidence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation 
 along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public L
 ibrary\, South Chapter and The William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor m
 ore information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada329a198b996a80a897bb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
