BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for Job Hunting: Build Your Own System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6a9b51a9aafa61002961b2a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Job hunting is a job in itself: applications\, deadlines\, int
 erviews\, follow-ups. What if you could build your own AI-powered system t
 o help you manage it?\nIn this hands-on class with our Innovator-in-Reside
 nce\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll explore a job-hunting dashboard built with AI
 : how it tracks applications\, sets automatic alerts for postings that mat
 ch you\, and practices interviews with you through role-play. You'll leave
  with the templates to build your own. We'll also talk about how employers
  screen applications\, and how it can make things unfair. Come explore a t
 ool that works for you\, not the other way around.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\
 , keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding exp
 erience required.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 202
 6 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of 
 the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be fille
 d on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you w
 ish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own U
 SB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes 
 activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nY
 ou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants 
 are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, w
 hich include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the p
 rivacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Co
 de\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn
  more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more 
 about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a9aafa61002961b2a1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Knitting Knot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T150000
UID:6ac40c5f9dbc2b002c8c88db@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come on over for a relaxing afternoon of knitting and crocheti
 ng. Join the knitting group where you can work on your own crochet and kni
 tting projects while enjoying great conversation. We'll swap tips\, techni
 ques\, patterns\, yarns and more!\nPlease note this is not a program where
  formal instructions are given. However\, we are happy to learn from each 
 other and help each other out where we can.\nAll levels are welcome. Bring
