DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
UID:6ab6cbfd6074830038298794@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever looked at a job posting and thought\, “I could
  never do that”? Or questioned whether you’re actually qualified\, eve
 n when your experience says otherwise? We’ll explore imposter syndrome a
 nd the self-doubt that can show up when applying for jobs\, starting a new
  role\, pursuing opportunities\, or stepping outside your comfort zone. Yo
 u’ll learn how to recognize common patterns of imposter syndrome\, and i
 dentify skills\, strengths\, and accomplishments you may be overlooking. W
 e’ll also explore how self-compassion can help you increase confidence a
 nd trust in yourself.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Res
 idence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation al
 ong with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Lib
 rary\, South Chapter and\nWilliam and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more i
 nformation\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
