BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Get Things Done with AI: Build Your Own Productivity System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T180000
UID:6a9b51af3b6c71003e5de7bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if your to-do list could check in on you\, notice what's 
 been stuck for weeks\, and offer to help instead of just sitting there?\nI
 n this class led by our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll e
 xplore a personal productivity system built around an AI agent and a weekl
 y-review practice. See how the agent loads goals\, counts what actually go
 t done\, flags the items that keep slipping\, and drafts next week's plan.
  It can support without cheerleading\, asking "Why has this been stuck for
  three weeks? Here are your options." You'll try it yourself with a practi
 ce set of goals\, and leave with the plain-text templates and a clearer ma
 p of how an AI might support you\, ready to build your own system at home.
 \nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are 
 provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and wi
 ll start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaran
 teed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remai
 ning seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capaci
 ty is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\,
  please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program
 \nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below
 ) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this
  program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance
  throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encou
 rage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending 
 this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy poli
 cy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogl
 e AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51af3b6c71003e5de7bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1 Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T180000
UID:6ab182a5129d8e0031f40d44@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Python and build your programming skills in a supportive
  group. This learning circle will meet on Monday evenings from November 2
  to December 7\, 4-6pm. Learning circles are study groups guided by staff
  for people who want to take a free online course together in a welcoming 
 space. Learners meet weekly and work together through the course materials
 . Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course and at
 tend all learning circle sessions.\nUsed by startups and tech giants like 
 Google\, Facebook\, Netflix\, and more\, Python offers you endless possibi
 lities for creating small and large-scale software projects. User-friendly
  with easy-to-read code\, Python is a great first programming language to 
 learn and requires no prior programming knowledge. Python skills open you 
 up to careers in almost any industry and are required if you want to conti
 nue to more advanced\, higher paying software development and engineering 
 roles such as software engineer\, systems administrator\, and security eng
 ineer.\nPython Essentials 1\nIn this course\, you will learn in-demand ski
 lls such as how to design\, develop\, and improve computer programs\, meth
 ods for analyzing problems using programming\, programming best practices\
 , and more. The course also prepares you for the PCEP – Certified Entry-
 Level Python Programmer certification (Exam PCEP-30-0x).\nFor more informa
 tion about the Python learning circle\, please contact\nnetworkingacademy@
 tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Brookbanks\, Lower Level Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab182a5129d8e0031f40d44
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
