BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Everyday Courage\, Everyday Resilience: Finding your resilient flo
 w in times of change and complexity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T140000
UID:6ada32998a335b6ae5c9f5ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive discussion with Career Coach in Res
 idence Sangeetha Dikshit and guest speaker\, Abirambika Ravivarman. Resili
 ence is more than bouncing back\, it's our capacity to navigate change\, u
 ncertainty\, and challenges with greater awareness\, adaptability\, and pu
 rpose. In this interactive session\, participants will explore the concept
  of Resilient Flow and how our beliefs\, habits\, and ways of making sense
  of the world influence how we respond under pressure.\nSangeetha Dikshit\
 n\, one of TPL's four Career Coaches in Residence. Sangeetha is a Career a
 nd Leadership Coach empowering individuals to navigate career transitions\
 , develop in-demand skills\, and achieve professional success.\nAbirambika
  Ravivarman\nis a Human-Centric Leadership and Systems Coach and the found
 er of Human Systems at Work. Her work goes beyond individual behaviour to
  focus on the deeper relational dynamics that shape team performance and c
 ulture. In today’s AI-augmented workplace\, she emphasizes the importanc
 e of strengthening the Human Edge—the presence-based and relational capa
 bilities that enable leaders and teams to thrive in complexity.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada32998a335b6ae5c9f5ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
