BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Housing Day: A Film Screening and Panel Discussion of See
 king Shelter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6abe6ad011bbf300684aa557@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:On November 24\nth\n\, join Homeless Connect Toronto at the To
 ronto Reference Library for a special premiere screening and community con
 versation celebrating the launch of Seeking Shelter\, a documentary series
  by filmmaker Nadine Valcin.\nAs Canada continues to grapple with a growin
 g housing crisis\, Seeking Shelter shines a light on the people\, organiza
 tions\, and grassroots movements creating innovative and inclusive solutio
 ns to housing instability. Through stories of resilience\, collaboration\,
  and community action\, the series explores what becomes possible when peo
 ple come together to reimagine housing.\nThis special event will feature p
 remiere screenings of:\nEpisode 2: Communal Land for the Common Good :\nTo
 ronto’s Parkdale Neighbourhood Land Trust is sowing the seeds for innova
 tive housing and communal growth.\nAnd\nEpisode 4: Co-ops and the Power of
  Community:\nSince the 1970s\, a Toronto co-operative has modelled a colla
 borative and people-first approach to housing.\nFollowing the screenings\,
  TVO's Nam Kiwanuka will moderate a panel discussion with housing subjec
 t-matter experts\, exploring the themes raised in the films and the future
  of community-driven housing solutions. Audience members will also have an
  opportunity to participate in a Q&A and contribute reflections to a colla
 borative poll. Panelists are: Nadine Valcin\, the award winning filmmaker
 \, Dominique Russell\, Executive Director of Kensington Market Community
  Land Trust\, and Steve Sirisko\, Board Member of Arcadia Housing Co-Op.
 \nDoors open: 6pm\nNo registration required.\nThe episodes are provided co
 urtesy of the National Film Board of Canada.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (1st floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe6ad011bbf300684aa557
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noirvember Film Screening: Double Indemnity (1944)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6ad7aa31901b02002cc3d073@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Noirvember is an annual\, month-long celebration of film noir.
  Join the Languages\, Literature\, and Fine Arts Department for a screeni
 ng of one of the defining works of the genre\, Billy Wilder's\nDouble Ind
 emnity\n(1944).\nAll are welcome. Drop-in until capacity is reached.\nRati
 ng: G\nRelease Year: 1944\nRunning Time: 107 minutes\nSynopsis (Audio Cin
 é Films):\nUnsuspecting Mr. Dietrichson becomes increasingly accident pro
 ne after his icily calculating wife encourages him to sign a double-indemn
 ity policy proposed by a smooth talking insurance agent. Against a backdro
 p of distinctly Californian settings\, the partners-in-crime plan the perf
 ect murder to collect on the insurance. Perfect until a claims manager get
 s a familiar feeling of foul play and pursues the matter relentlessly. Ten
 sion soars as the would-be lovers find themselves plotting against each ot
 her.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7aa31901b02002cc3d073
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
