BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T200000
UID:6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class led by our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRy
 an Kelln\n\, you'll learn "vibe-coding": using an AI coding assistant to 
 build your own interactive story or simple game. You'll design the branche
 s\, describe the rules in plain language\, test for the tricky edge cases 
 (what if the player picks the weird option?)\, and end up with a single fi
 le you can share with anyone. Just a story you want to tell. This is the p
 layful sibling of the practical vibe-coding workshop.\nPrerequisites: Mou
 se\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding 
 experience required.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 
 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes 
 of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be fi
 lled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf yo
 u wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your ow
 n USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includ
 es activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.
 \nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipan
 ts are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\
 , which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review th
 e privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude
  Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\
 nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection 
 Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto
  Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, 
 and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registr
 ation\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
