BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Short History of Library Architecture in Toronto and Beyond
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T200000
UID:6adbc6957b0eb473bbdb27b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Christopher Hume\, the architecture critic and urban issues co
 lumnist of the Toronto Star\, presents a short history of library architec
 ture. He will be commenting on the structures and social relevance of monu
 mental libraries from Paris\, Boston\, New York\, with a focus on Toronto 
 Public Libraries from around the city.\nHume is the recipient of 2009 The 
 National Newspaper Award for journalism in architecture and urban affairs.
  His illustrious career at the Toronto Star earned him a President’s Awa
 rd for Architectural Journalism from the Royal Architectural Institute of 
 Canada. Hume's book\, William James’ Toronto Views\, won a Toronto Herit
 age Award in 2000 and in 2004 he received a Landscape Ontario award.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adbc6957b0eb473bbdb27b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
