DESCRIPTION:John Ota presents​ and discusses his book\,\nThe Dining Room
  : Exploring the Design of Twelve Iconic Rooms in Search of the Perfect Di
 ning Experience.​\n​(Random House\, 2026).\nExplore the stories behind
  twelve iconic dining rooms in homes around the world—from a Japanese sa
 murai house to Claude Monet's brilliant yellow dining room to Frida Kahlo'
 s Casa Azul to Jackie Kennedy’s White House—and travel through time in
  pursuit of the ultimate design.​\nThe Dining Room is an englightening a
 nd joyous celebration of history\, culture and the art of dning. Presenter
  John Ota's charming observations of the surprising impact of dining rooms
  on our lives and the cherised moments we share within them will delight a
 rmchair travellers\, history fanatics and interior design enthusiasts alik
 e.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
