SUMMARY:Resume Development and Modern Job Search Techniques
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T143000
UID:6ac5142d29c3d600332e0473@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This session will help participants create stronger\, more com
 petitive resumes by learning the key components of an effective resume and
  strategies for standing out to employers. Participants will explore diffe
 rent resume formats and when to use them\, learn how to tailor resume cont
 ent to highlight their strengths\, and gain an understanding of applicant 
 tracking systems (ATS) and other hiring technologies. The session will als
 o cover common resume mistakes and practical ways to correct them\, ensuri
 ng participants can present their skills and experience in the most effect
 ive way possible.\nThis workshop is presented by ACCES Employment Toronto\
 , focused on supporting jobseekers and employers with a variety of special
 ized programs and resources both in-person and online.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac5142d29c3d600332e0473
