BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch: Chris Ware's The Acme Novelty Library #21
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T200000
UID:6af32ec0bb58d8cbdfcfdd2e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Torontonians: You are cordially invited to join Chris Ware as 
 he awkwardly acknowledges the release of THE ACME NOVELTY LIBRARY #21. War
 e will be in conversation with fellow cartoonist Seth (Palookaville 25).\n
 Books will be available for purchase from The Beguiling–the official boo
 kseller for this event.\nChris Ware\nis a writer and artist and has contri
 buted graphic fiction and thirty-two covers to\nThe New Yorker\nsince 1999
 . He is the author of\nJimmy Corrigan: The Smartest Kid on Earth\n\, which
  won the Guardian First Book Award in 2001\;\nBuilding Stories\n\, which w
 as chosen as a Top 10 fiction book by both\nthe Times\nand\nTime\nin 2012\
 ; and\nRusty Brown\nwhich was a finalist for the PEN/Jean Stein award and 
 named among the\nNew York Times\n’ top 100 Books of 2019. His work has b
 een exhibited at the Hammer Museum\, the Museum of Contemporary Art Chicag
 o\, and the Whitney Museum of American Art\, as well as at the Adam Baumgo
 ld Gallery in New York and the Galerie Martel in Paris. In 2021\, Ware rec
 eived the Grand Prix de la Ville d’Angoulême and a solo retrospective o
 f his work was presented at the Centre Pompidou in 2022\, traveling on to 
 venues in Switzerland\, Italy\, Holland\, and Spain\, before making its on
 ly US appearance in May 2026 at the Billy Ireland Library and Museum in Co
 lumbus\, Ohio.\nSeth\nis a cartoonist\, designer\, and collector. His book
 s include\nWimbledon Green\, George Sprott\,\nand\nClyde Fans\n. He is cur
 rently working on a long graphic novel that will appear in the years to co
 me. He lives in Guelph\, Ontario with his beloved wife Tania and two cats 
 (Albert and Arthur) in an old house he has pretentiously named “Inkwell
 ’s End.” He was born in 1962 and is increasingly feeling lost in this 
 modern world.\nPraise for Chris Ware\n"Chris Ware has built a career as a 
 sort of astronaut exploring the nature of the consciousness."—\nNew York
  Times\n“Maximalist and spare.”—\nWashington Post\n“Nobody chronic
 les lives of quiet desperation with the exacting meticulousness of Chris W
 are.”—\nNPR\nThe Library of Acme Novelty in Fifty-two Volumes\nACME No
 velty Library\nJimmy Corrigan\nPalookaville
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af32ec0bb58d8cbdfcfdd2e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
