DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
UID:6af614ec22b92c0041a95dae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:From Impostor Syndrome to Self-Leadership is an interactive wo
 rkshop that helps young professionals build confidence\, trust themselves 
 and take their place in their personal and professional lives. Participant
 s will explore how self-doubt and impostor syndrome can hold them back\, t
 hen learn practical ways to recognize their strengths\, reframe limiting b
 eliefs\, and take strategic action to create the opportunities they desire
 .\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is genero
 usly supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting 
 donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter
  and\nThe William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, ple
 ase visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and partic
 ipating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement
