UID:6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop with our 
 Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll use an AI coding assistant
  to build your own small\, useful webpage\, checklist\, or organizer from 
 scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe what you want\, review the 
 plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bugs\, and write documentatio
 n so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, key
 boarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experien
 ce required.\nRegistration is required and will start November 9\, 2026 at
  12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the 
 start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on
  a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish 
 to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB s
 tick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes acti
 vities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou d
 o not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are 
 encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which
  include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the priva
 cy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\n
 Learn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn 
 more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:
 \nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public
  Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(
