BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Interview Jitters to Interview Confidence: Navigating In-Pers
 on\, Virtual and AI-Powered Interviews
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T193000
UID:6aeb8cb35ea4c386b3ec9aa5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interview formats are evolving\, but the ability to communicat
 e your experience\, value and potential with confidence remains essential.
  This practical webinar will help job seekers prepare for in-person\, virt
 ual and increasingly common AI-powered interviews.\nParticipants will lear
 n how to manage interview anxiety\, structure clear and compelling respons
 es\, communicate effectively on camera and adapt their approach to differe
 nt interview formats. We will also explore what employers and recruiters a
 ssess during interviews\, common mistakes to avoid\, and how candidates ca
 n remain authentic and human throughout a technology-enabled hiring proces
 s.\nAttendees will leave with practical strategies to approach their next 
 interview with greater clarity\, preparation and confidence.\nSpeaker Bio\
 n- Wagisha Singh is a Talent Acquisition Specialist with over six years of
  experience recruiting across Canada and the United States. She has partne
 red with organizations ranging from growing businesses to large national e
 mployers\, hiring talent across logistics\, transportation\, supply chain\
 , skilled trades\, healthcare\, accounting and finance\, operations\, and 
 leadership roles.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residen
 ce and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along 
 with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library
 \, South Chapter and\nThe William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more i
 nformation\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb8cb35ea4c386b3ec9aa5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
